  "scientific_scope": "Prospective four-channel NIRPS_V3_3 near-infrared (0.98-1.80 um YJH) and unified panchromatic (0.38-1.80 um) narrowband laser technosignature survey across 152 ESO 3.6 m NIRPS_HE (R = 70,000, simultaneous Fiber B = SKY) Phase-3 exposures of 22 nearby FGKM stars (27 CONTROL exposures across 4 verified zero-planet stars HD184509, GJ707, GJ643, GJ3618 + 125 SCIENCE exposures across 18 confirmed exoplanet hosts at 1.302-38.57 pc, including 5 single-night 12-exposure transit time-series campaigns, 11 brand-new solar-neighborhood exoplanet hosts, and the <2 pc ESPRESSO+NIRPS panchromatic bridge on Proxima Centauri and Barnard's Star). Incorporates native HITRAN atmospheric transmission & pre/post-telluric consistency (Gate G2_V33), NIST chromospheric mask & D081-motivated cross-star molecular bandhead ridge veto (Gate G3_V33), Fiber-B sky-subtraction & 71-order overlap verification (Gate G4_V33), Hawaii-2RG 11-px LSF / IPC hot-pixel / persistence gate (Gate G5_V33), direct two-band Cohen et al. (2003) 2MASS (J, H) radiometric calibration across 9 YJH bands (including 1064.1 nm Nd:YAG/Yb and 1550.0 nm Er C-band), and a unified 80-unique-star (501-exposure, 29 stars <10 pc) D079+D080+D081+D082 Panchromatic V3 Synthesis.",
